<article class="env-lemma" id="0EUP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EUP">Lemma <span data-tag="0EUP">29.48.4</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme. The following are equivalent: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The scheme $X$ is seminormal. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
For every affine open $U \subset X$ the ring $\mathcal{O}_ X(U)$ is seminormal. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
There exists an affine open covering $X = \bigcup U_ i$ such that each $\mathcal{O}_ X(U_ i)$ is seminormal. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
There exists an open covering $X = \bigcup X_ j$ such that each open subscheme $X_ j$ is seminormal. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Moreover, if $X$ is seminormal then every open subscheme is seminormal. The same statements are true with “seminormal” replaced by “absolutely weakly normal”. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Properties, Lemma <a href="/tag/01OR" data-tag="01OR">28.4.3</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/0EUM" data-tag="0EUM">29.48.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>